=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
The Apache2 HTTP server on `srv1` (IP 10.5.0.4) was stopped and is sitting `inactive (dead)` despite being enabled for autostart. BIND (named) is running correctly on the same host, the zone `jeremysitlab.com` is authoritative with a wildcard A record pointing every campus hostname to 10.5.0.4, and client resolvers are correctly pointed at 10.5.0.4. DNS resolution itself works: `nslookup srv1.jeremysitlab.com` from both `pc2` and `pc3` returns the right address. The failure occurs one layer up: when the browser attempts an HTTP TCP connection to port 80 on 10.5.0.4, it is refused because nothing is listening (confirmed via `ss -tlnp` — no port-80 entry — and `curl` exit code 7 from `pc3`). Users experience this as "site can't be found" because many browsers surface a TCP connection failure with language similar to a DNS failure. The Apache configuration passes `configtest` with no errors and `/var/www/html/index.html` is present, so there is no config or content issue. The root cause is that the `apache2` service was stopped on `srv1`, taking the only internal web server offline. The corrective fix is a single command executed on `srv1`: `systemctl start apache2`, which will immediately bring port 80 back up and restore all campus-hostname website access for office clients.
=== END ===